11. DONOR AVAILABILITY POLICY — CRITICAL TEST AREA

The default waiting period must remain three calendar months, not 90 days.

The canonical policy document should be:

systemSettings/availabilityPolicy

Expected default fields:

minimumIntervalMonths: 3

policyVersion

updatedAt

updatedBy

Check that only users with:

settings.availability_policy.manage

can update the policy.

Verify that every successful policy change creates a trustworthy audit event containing the actor, action, previous value, new value, policy version, timestamp, and outcome.

Use a trusted backend and server-generated timestamps for policy changes and audit records.

Required date tests

Test:

Donation date of January 15: eligibility on April 15 under the default policy.

Donation date of January 31: documented month-end handling.

Donation date of November 30: correct handling across year boundaries.

Donation dates around February 28 and February 29.

Leap-year transitions.

The day before eligibility.

The exact eligibility date.

The day after eligibility.

Bangladesh-local date boundaries.

Different browser timezone settings.

Missing donation date.

Invalid or future donation date.

Donor updates the last donation date.

Policy changes from three months to another permitted interval.

Search results after a policy change.

Donor explicitly chooses unavailable.

Donor becomes suspended or deactivated.

Donor is unverified, pending, or rejected.

Forged eligibilityDate or calculatedAvailability.

Imported records containing forged status values.

Document and enforce one consistent month-end rule. For example, if the target month has no equivalent day, clamp the eligibility date to the final day of that month.

Use the Asia/Dhaka calendar date for eligibility comparisons. Prevent off-by-one errors caused by converting date-only values to UTC timestamps.

Availability must be calculated from trusted data and the current approved policy.

A scheduled job must not be required for accurate search results.

A manual unavailable choice must not be overridden simply because the waiting period has passed.

Do not mark donors with missing donation dates as eligible automatically.

Do not describe software availability as medical certification.

